`@styles` gives you six ready-made inline style fragments for the `style` slots on `@html` helpers. Each fragment folds into the surrounding HTML string during compilation and adds no runtime code.

### Using the fragments in `.mtf` files

`.mtf` files see the constants by bare name because both `@html` and `@styles` supply the fixed template prelude:

[codeblock, $code "text":
    [h1, center: A centred heading.]
]

The fragment fills the helper's `style` slot. The same constants are available under every builder, not only HTML projects.

### Binding in `.moth` files

A `.moth` file needs an explicit dependency clause:

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    @styles center, larger
]

### The six exports

- `center` produces `text-align: center;`
- `right` produces `text-align: right;`
- `left` produces `text-align: left;`
- `smaller` produces `font-size: smaller;`
- `medium` produces `font-size: medium;`
- `larger` produces `font-size: larger;`

For the full export table and prelude rules see @#styles-helpers (@styles advanced).
